#EXCELSIOR! NewUser CallBack Validation Utility

#Put in all the numbers that you want the system to be able to call back.
#You must have the area/country code before the prefix!
#To allow the system to call back ANY NUMBER, make the first entry an '*'.

#If the areacode's match with the system's default, the system will call
#prefix-phonenumber,  else it will call 1-areacode-prefix-phonenumber.

#To allow the system to call back any number in a specific area code enter
#the areacode followed by an asterisk (*).  313* would call all numbers in
#the 313 areacode

#To lock out an areacode if system is set to call any number, put that area
#code and a minus.  900- would not let the system call any user that has 
#their area code as 900 (bogus).

#To stop calls to a prefix place a - (minus) before the prefix

#To use prefix ranges, use AREACODE|FIRST-LAST
#313|771-779  will allow the system to call back all numbers in the 313 area-
#             code between the exchanges 771 and 779.

#The AccessGroup to be given to the user upon successful validation.
2

#No calls to 911 Emergency ;-)
-911

#stops all 900 AREACODE calls (only if set to call ANY NUMBER)
900-

#Example:  (only call 313-772 exchange)
#313-772
